#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Bundle a versioned JS distribution for the root workbench package while keeping the repo's source-TS development flow intact."
 ~#taste: "correctness, layering, release clarity"
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-20 14:42] observe — the root package still exports source .ts entrypoints and the current build only typechecks; there is no versioned JS dist artifact yet.
 >>[2026-03-20 14:42] decide — the first slice should produce a dedicated dist/release artifact without flipping the workspace's live resolution over to dist.
 >>[2026-03-20 14:42] observe — plain tsc emit is not enough because the current source graph depends on workspace-only aliases like @spw/cli and @spw/seed.
 >>[2026-03-20 14:42] taste — version truth should stay anchored in the root package manifest, with dist manifests derived from that source of truth.
 >>[2026-03-20 14:48] implement — added a JS dist builder that bundles the root public runtime/CLI entrypoints into dist/, rewrites the CLI shebang to node, and stamps dist/package.json from the root version.
 >>[2026-03-20 14:52] decide — the first dist artifact is runtime-JS only; declaration publishing remains a later hardening slice rather than a blocker for beginning JS release bundling.
 >>[2026-03-20 14:54] implement — wired bundle:jsdist and release bundling so source, JS dist, docs, and extensions land under release/v<version>/.
 >>[2026-03-20 14:55] surprise — bundle-release initially failed because the new shell script was invoked directly without an executable bit; switching the orchestrator to explicit bash invocation made the flow robust against file-mode drift.
 >>[2026-03-20 14:56] verify — build:jsdist, bundle:jsdist, node dist/bin/spw.js help, tar inspection of spw-js-dist, and bundle:release -- --skip-build --best-effort all passed.
}

